&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About commercetools&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Real innovation starts with a strong foundation, and at commercetools, that comes from the perfect balance of our product and our people.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Behind every leap forward is a collective of builders, explorers, doers, makers, and problem-solvers. The kind of people who not only created composable commerce but also shaped the culture of experimentation that idea unlocked. Together they are the engine of commerce innovation today.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At commercetools, we power the next era of commerce for our customers. Whether it’s AI-driven solutions that help enterprises make smarter business decisions, bridging digital and physical shopping experiences, or enabling entirely new ways for industries to connect with their customers, we help the world’s most ambitious companies experiment, scale, and grow without limits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here the best idea wins, not the loudest voice. You will have the tools, trust, and space to not only build the future of commerce, but to build your own.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Über unser Customer Success Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hallo! Ich bin &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/in/enricocellini/&quot;&gt;Enrico&lt;/a&gt;, Customer Success Team Lead bei commercetools. Mein Team konzentriert sich auf den Aufbau langfristiger, beratungsorientierter Partnerschaften mit unseren Enterprise-Kunden.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Unser Customer Success Team gestaltet und skaliert mit Leidenschaft eine außergewöhnliche Upmarket Customer Experience im gesamten Enterprise-Segment. Im Zuge unseres weiteren Wachstums freuen wir uns darauf, unser Team in EMEA um eine:n &lt;strong&gt;Senior Customer Success Manager (m/w/d)&lt;/strong&gt; zu erweitern.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In dieser Rolle bilden Sie das entscheidende Bindeglied zwischen unseren Kunden und den modernsten Commerce-Produkten auf dem Markt. Sie betreuen unsere größten und komplexesten Enterprise-Kunden – von schnell wachsenden Marken bis hin zu börsennotierten Unternehmen. Dabei konzentrieren Sie sich auf Account Health, die Post-Sales-Adoption und die Positionierung von commercetools als vertrauenswürdigen strategischen Partner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sie arbeiten eng mit unseren internen Support-, Produkt- und Vertriebsteams zusammen, um optimale Voraussetzungen für den Erfolg unserer Kunden zu schaffen. Da commercetools leistungsstark, modern und hochgradig flexibel ist, setzen Sie Ihr tiefes technisches Verständnis, Ihre Vertriebsaffinität und Ihre erstklassigen Kommunikationsfähigkeiten ein, um große Marken bei der Gestaltung außergewöhnlicher Commerce-Workflows zu unterstützen und langfristigen Mehrwert zu schaffen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Über das Account Management hinaus tragen Sie aktiv dazu bei, unsere Customer-Success-Praxis sowohl regional als auch global mitzugestalten und weiterzuentwickeln.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Wenn Sie bereit sind, innovative Lösungen für bekannte Marken voranzutreiben, die Kundenkommunikation über verschiedene Kanäle hinweg zu steuern und in einer einflussreichen Rolle aufzublühen, freuen wir uns darauf, Sie kennenzulernen!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Der Interviewprozess für diese Position findet auf Englisch statt. Wir suchen daher eine Person, die sowohl auf Deutsch als auch auf Englisch sicher mit unseren Kunden kommunizieren kann.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ihre Mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie begleiten Enterprise-Kunden dabei, den Mehrwert unserer Agentic-Commerce-Architektur – einschließlich Composable Commerce, Frontend und Connect – zu maximieren und flexible, zukunftssichere Tech-Stacks aufzubauen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie übersetzen neue Produktfeatures und -funktionen in klare Geschäftsergebnisse und stimmen diese direkt auf die strategischen Ziele und zentralen ROI-Kennzahlen des jeweiligen Kunden ab.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie treiben Kundenbeziehungen proaktiv voran und leiten wirkungsvolle Strategic Business Reviews (SBRs), um die Kundenbindung zu stärken, die Plattformnutzung zu steigern und langfristiges Wachstum zu beschleunigen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie arbeiten eng mit dem Produktmanagement zusammen, vertreten die Bedürfnisse unserer Kunden und liefern entscheidendes Feedback, das die Roadmap unserer neuesten Produktinnovationen mitgestaltet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie arbeiten nahtlos und teamübergreifend mit Sales, Product und Support zusammen, bringen tiefgehendes technisches und kaufmännisches Know-how ein und sichern so langfristig den Erfolg unserer Enterprise-Kunden.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie repräsentieren commercetools in Webinaren, Kundenfallstudien und Beratungsgremien, um Kundenerfolge sichtbar zu machen und das Engagement innerhalb der Community zu fördern.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie übernehmen eine zentrale Rolle bei der Weiterentwicklung globaler Customer-Success-Frameworks, treiben interne Prozessverbesserungen voran und gestalten die langfristige operative Strategie der Abteilung mit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie agieren intern und extern als anerkannte:r Fachexpert:in, unterstützen Teammitglieder als Mentor:in, fördern die funktionsübergreifende Zusammenarbeit und tragen dazu bei, die gemeinsamen Standards unserer Customer-Success-Praxis weiter anzuheben.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie fungieren als Eskalationsinstanz und arbeiten mit dem Product-Support-Team zusammen, um Probleme schnell zu lösen. Auch in anspruchsvollen Eskalationssituationen bleiben Sie ruhig, professionell und besonnen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Was Sie mitbringen – Ihr Profil&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mindestens fünf Jahre Erfahrung in einem High-Touch-Tech-Umfeld mit nachweisbaren Erfolgen im Bereich Customer Success, Pre-Sales oder Technical Consulting – idealerweise in den Branchen E-Commerce oder Retail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deutschkenntnisse auf muttersprachlichem Niveau sowie verhandlungssichere Englischkenntnisse&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ein tiefes technisches Verständnis moderner API-first- und Headless-Technologien, gepaart mit betriebswirtschaftlichem Denken und der Fähigkeit, komplexe Technologien in messbaren ROI zu übersetzen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Die Fähigkeit, als überzeugende:r und vertrauenswürdige:r Berater:in aufzutreten, Gespräche auf C-Level-Ebene zu führen, Kundenstrategien mitzugestalten und Expansionspotenziale sicher zu identifizieren und zu erschließen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eine strukturierte und agile Arbeitsweise sowie die Fähigkeit, komplexe Accounts über globale, funktionsübergreifende Teams hinweg eigenverantwortlich zu betreuen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eine teamorientierte Persönlichkeit, die in einer dynamischen, internationalen Tech-Kultur aufblüht, sowie eine Reisebereitschaft von bis zu 50 %, um wertvolle Kundenbeziehungen aufzubauen und zu pflegen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Von Vorteil:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Weitere Sprachkenntnisse (Französisch oder Spanisch)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Because work and life are connected, our benefits are too. We’ve designed them to give you the security, flexibility, and opportunities you need to focus on what matters most.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🩺 &lt;strong&gt;Comprehensive health benefits&lt;/strong&gt; for you and your dependents, including access to OpenUp for personalized mental health support&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📚 &lt;strong&gt;Learning and development &lt;/strong&gt;opportunities including an annual learning budget, access to self-paced learning platforms and language training, personalized coaching, mentorship, and leadership programs&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🍼 &lt;strong&gt;Family Leave Plus&lt;/strong&gt; gives you additional fully paid weeks of parental leave on top of government-provided leave, so you can spend more time with your new addition&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📈 &lt;strong&gt;Our equity participation program&lt;/strong&gt; allows you to share in our success&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information on our benefits, &lt;a href=&quot;https://commercetools.com/careers/our-benefits&quot;&gt;visit this page.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come as you are. Build with us.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your unique perspective is essential to our success. We are committed to building a team that reflects the world around us because we know it’s the only way to build the future. We celebrate our differences and have created a hiring process that’s fair, inclusive, and designed to let your talent shine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We proudly welcome applicants of every race, color, religion, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, and any other part of your identity that makes you who you are. As an equal opportunity employer, we believe that our strength lies in our diversity, and we invite you to be a part of our global community.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information on our diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging practices, &lt;a href=&quot;https://commercetools.com/careers/dei-esg&quot;&gt;visit this page&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Samsara (NYSE: IOT) is the pioneer of the Connected Operations™ Cloud, which is a platform that enables organizations that depend on physical operations to harness Internet of Things (IoT) data to develop actionable insights and improve their operations. At Samsara, we are helping improve the safety, efficiency and sustainability of the physical operations that power our global economy. Representing more than 40% of global GDP, these industries are the infrastructure of our planet, including agriculture, construction, field services, transportation, and manufacturing — and we are excited to help digitally transform their operations at scale.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Working at Samsara means you’ll help define the future of physical operations and be on a team that’s shaping an exciting array of product solutions, including Video-Based Safety, Vehicle Telematics, Apps and Driver Workflows, and Equipment Monitoring. As part of a recently public company, you’ll have the autonomy and support to make an impact as we build for the long term.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Account Development Representative (ADR) at Samsara, you will be trained — both on the job and through formal programs led by a world-class Sales team — to take on your next role as a closing Account Executive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On a daily basis, you will build and work a portfolio of target accounts for our EMEA business in France: researching each account for commercial signal, prioritising which contacts to approach and in what order, and running a connected, multi-touch outbound motion that generates qualified pipeline rather than one-off meetings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a remote position open to candidates based in France and the United Kingdom. This position requires working hours in CET. Relocation assistance will not be provided for this role.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You should apply if:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You want to impact the industries that run our world:&lt;/strong&gt; your efforts will result in real-world impact — helping to keep the lights on, get food into grocery stores, and ensure workers return home safely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are the architect of your own career:&lt;/strong&gt; if you put in the work, this role won&#39;t be your last at Samsara. Successful ADRs can see promotion to a closing role in two years or less.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’re excited by AI:&lt;/strong&gt; you’ll use cutting-edge AI tools every day and sell some of the most advanced AI in the physical operations space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You think several moves ahead:&lt;/strong&gt; you&#39;d rather build a real relationship across an account than force a single contact to a decision they&#39;re not ready to make.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have an innate curiosity about how businesses work:&lt;/strong&gt; one day you&#39;ll be researching a transport operator, the next a food distribution centre. Our best reps dig into the businesses they support to make a sharper case for why Samsara matters to them specifically.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You treat rejection as a learning experience:&lt;/strong&gt; in this role you will get hung up on and told no. You need the resilience to prepare, call again, and adjust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You want to be with the best:&lt;/strong&gt; Samsara&#39;s high-performance Sales culture means you&#39;ll be surrounded by the best and challenged to go further than you have before.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research target accounts before outreach — pulling commercial signal out of public information (financials, news, hiring activity, compliance or safety pressure) to build a specific, defensible point of view on where Samsara adds value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and prioritise an account-level contact plan, identifying who to approach first across a range of stakeholders (e.g. MD, Operations/Transport Manager, Compliance/H&amp;amp;S, Finance) and being able to justify that choice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run a connected, multi-touch outbound motion across phone, email and LinkedIn — using early conversations to gather information and multi-thread the account, not just to book a meeting at any cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write personalised, researched outreach (including cold emails) that carries a specific point of view into every call, rather than working from a generic script.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Read what a contact gives you on the call and adapt in real time — including recognising when the right move is to gather information and position a follow-up with someone else, rather than push for a meeting the contact can&#39;t actually commit to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep meticulous account and contact records in Salesforce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become a product expert and represent the Samsara brand at trade shows and events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements for the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1–3 years professional experience, ideally in customer-facing roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6–12 months&amp;nbsp; experience in a sales or equivalent target driven role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly motivated and committed, with a strong desire to work in target-driven sales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of consistently meeting or exceeding targets in previous roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, both verbal and written&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious, and able to ask insightful questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A champion of a Growth Mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly proficient in English and fluent in French&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI literacy and ability to showcase examples of leveraging AI in your work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An ideal candidate also has:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort turning unstructured information (an annual report, a website, a news article) into a clear commercial argument&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience multi-threading or navigating multiple stakeholders within a single sale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine willingness to prepare — to research and write — before a call, rather than relying on improvising well under pressure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in closing-sales roles or similar target driven environment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of achievement beyond work (e.g. academics, sports, charity)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to collaborate and influence in a &quot;win as a team&quot; environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excitement about solving new problems in innovative ways&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motivation to help build a fast-growing business in the IoT and SaaS space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADR pathways&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Through Samsara&#39;s ADR program, there are always opportunities to move to the next level and take on more responsibility. With emphasis on continued professional development, training doesn&#39;t stop after onboarding — we provide opportunities to expand ADRs&#39; understanding of the market and competitors, develop hard skills, and work with mentors to progress through three levels:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADR I&lt;/strong&gt; — focus on inbound leads: a high volume of conversations, sharing the ins and outs of our products, and fostering relationships with interested prospects. Learning opportunities include call sessions with senior Sales team members, tool training (Salesforce, Salesloft, Lusha), product knowledge, and objection handling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADR II&lt;/strong&gt; — work on top-of-funnel movement, creating high-quality sales engagements, and supporting Account Executives. Enrolled in specialised training including professional writing, persona-based messaging, cold calling 2.0, and AE collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADR III&lt;/strong&gt; — work hand-in-hand with field Account Executives and Enterprise Regional Sales Managers. Partner on large accounts, implement territory plans, join weekly strategy meetings, and schedule/attend customer demos, alongside a mentorship program ahead of an AE interview.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please submit an English CV with your application.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Total Rewards&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Samsara, we build for the people who keep the global economy moving. We want owners, not passengers, which is why &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.samsara.com/company/careers/benefits&quot;&gt;our rewards&lt;/a&gt; are designed to fuel high-impact builders. Our compensation program delivers above-market total compensation through a combination of base salary, performance-based bonus/variable pay, and equity (for eligible roles) in a high-growth public company. We meaningfully differentiate pay for our top performers, who have the opportunity to earn above-market compensation that can outpace the broader market over time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beyond compensation, we provide the foundations that enable long-term success: a flexible, employee-led remote model, a professional development stipend, comprehensive health and parental leave plans, and more. If you’re ready to build for the long term and own the outcome, your journey starts here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible Working&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Samsara, we embrace a flexible working model that caters to the diverse needs of our teams. Our offices are open for those who prefer to work in-person and we also support remote work where it aligns with our operational requirements. For certain positions, being close to one of our offices or within a specific geographic area is important to facilitate collaboration, access to resources, or alignment with our service regions. In these cases, the job description will clearly indicate any working location requirements. Our goal is to ensure that all members of our team can contribute effectively, whether they are working on-site, in a hybrid model, or fully remotely. All offers of employment are contingent upon an individual’s ability to secure and maintain the legal right to work at the company and in the specified work location, if applicable.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Belonging at Samsara&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Samsara, we welcome everyone regardless of their background. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, protected veteran status, disability, age, and other characteristics protected by law. We depend on the unique approaches of our team members to help us solve complex problems and want to ensure that Samsara is a place where people from all backgrounds can make an impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Samsara is an inclusive work environment, and we are committed to ensuring equal opportunity in employment for qualified persons with disabilities. Please email &lt;a ---------- or &lt;a href=&quot;https://forms.gle/DrM6DFQUiSgfPtCVA&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; if you require any reasonable accommodations throughout the recruiting process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Authenticity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We use &lt;a href=&quot;https://hiretofu.com/privacyPolicy&quot;&gt;Tofu&lt;/a&gt;, a fraud detection tool, to validate the authenticity of applications and protect against identity fraud. This ensures we are connecting with real people and allows us to prioritize genuine candidates. Please see Samsara’s &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.samsara.com/legal/candidate-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; for more information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fraudulent Employment Offers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Samsara is aware of scams involving fake job interviews and offers. Please know we do not charge fees to applicants at any stage of the hiring process. Official communication about your application will only come from emails ending in ----- ----- or ----- For more information regarding fraudulent employment offers, please visit our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://samsara.com/blog/avoiding-fake-job-offers&quot;&gt;blog post here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div data-ogsc=&quot;black&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ogsc=&quot;&quot; data-ogsb=&quot;yellow&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-ogsc=&quot;&quot; data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;About Acadia Pharmaceuticals&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div data-ogsc=&quot;black&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div data-ogsc=&quot;black&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ogsc=&quot;&quot; data-ogsb=&quot;yellow&quot;&gt;Acadia is committed to turning scientific promise into meaningful innovation that makes the difference for underserved neurological and rare disease communities around the world. Our commercial portfolio includes the first and only FDA-approved treatments for Parkinson’s disease psychosis and Rett syndrome. We are developing the next wave of therapeutic advancements with a robust and diverse pipeline that includes mid- to late-stage programs in Alzheimer’s disease psychosis and Lewy body dementia psychosis, along with earlier-stage programs that address other underserved patient needs. At Acadia, we’re here to be their difference.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Position Summary&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Sr. Medical Director, Germany will lead the development and execution of the local medical affairs strategy together with the field Medical Science Liaisons (MSLs) and in line with the European Medical Affairs strategy and the local country strategy for RETT syndrome including the integrated medical plans with full medical budget ownership and responsibility. Responsibilities will include building and maintaining external stakeholder relationships and collaborations, as well as continuing to position Acadia as a thought leader and valued partner with patient advocacy groups (PAG) and medical/scientific RETT community in Germany. This individual will be responsible for the effectiveness and compliance of scientific exchange conducted to meet the needs of clinicians, patient advocates, and other key external and internal stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Primary Responsibilities&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide scientific and medical leadership, including development of strategic country medical affairs (post-launch) plans, identifying specific unmet medical needs, and data gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading the local medical affairs team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure strong medical/scientific leadership in coordination and participation in country MRC/MLR procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish appropriate strategic partnerships with Centers of Excellence, KOLs, and PAGs, in areas of scientific interest.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure aligned and close cross-functional collaboration, with country GM, Market Access, other relevant country and international staff to optimally manage relationships and ensure alignment and effective execution of the German medical strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and ensure operational medical excellence, in collaboration with EU medical teams and aligned with country strategy, to capture and track key medical tactics and medical (post-launch) activities in Germany.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide medical expertise and editorial support in data dissemination at conferences and in medical journals, as appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Involvement with key HCPs in the exchange of scientific and medical information including Advisory Boards and presentations at national meetings and conferences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain, together with MSLs, close professional relationships with KOLs and emerging scientific leaders in the community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee gathering and reporting field medical insights through existing Veeva CRM system and in line with company rules and requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee and communicate to cross-functional stakeholders the insights the MSL team gains about competitive landscape, unmet needs of physicians and advocacy groups. Develops potential actionable plans to address these local insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manages publication activities, including review and approval of abstracts and manuscripts, local publication strategy and real-world evidence development and compliant collaboration with authors, as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Education/Experience/Skills&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MD highly preferred; PhD, PharmD, or an equivalent qualification may also be considered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of Medical Affairs leadership experience in the biopharmaceutical industry in Germany or the DACH region; broader regional experience is advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior team-management experience is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Substantial rare-disease—preferably neurological—experience in Germany and/or the DACH region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive knowledge of the German healthcare system and applicable national rules and regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience coordinating and participating in national MLR/MRC procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging with rare-disease patient advocacy groups is highly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Skills&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive knowledge to critically appraise studies and clinical evidence to allow engagement on higher scientific level with HCPs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In depth understanding of compliance and regulatory requirements, including extensive personal experience and expertise with MRC/MLR procedures, for pharmaceutical Medical Affairs, R&amp;amp;D and Commercial activities in Germany.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, collaboration, and presentation skills, and experience in the delivery of scientific presentations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agile, independent and proactive working style.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personal sense of purpose, confidence, and stand fest in challenging situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build strong cross-functional and cross-company relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to collaborate and share information to contribute to the planning process and execute the agreed local Medical (pre)launch plan, together with MSL team, and in line with Regional Medical Affairs strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in German at native or near-native level and strong English proficiency are required, with the ability to communicate complex details clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel both locally and internationally is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;#NC1 #LI-HYBRID&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;What we offer US-based Employees:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive base, bonus, new hire and ongoing equity packages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, dental, and vision insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employer-paid life, disability, business travel and EAP coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) Plan with a fully vested company match 1:1 up to 5%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Stock Purchase Plan with a 2-year purchase price lock-in&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ vacation days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;13 -15 paid holidays, including office closure between December 24th and January 1st&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10 days of paid sick time&lt;/li&gt;
